The Configure method
When a request comes into ASP.NET Core, it goes through what is called
the request/response pipeline, where some middleware code is executed. This pipeline is
configured using a method called Configure. It is this method we will use to define
exactly which middleware is executed and in what order. Middleware code is invoked by
methods that generally start with Use in the app parameter. So, we would typically specify
middleware such as authentication early in the Configure method, and MVC middleware
toward the end. The pipeline that the template created is as follows:
